db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105934"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32671/selection/9162a6f6012cb98addd8a583acc316883bc4458aaa2d646ae20ba3e2c826df8c" :answer/id #uuid "d0a59a72-0496-52b9-841f-b8710c7cc3bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32671/selection/0d70bb18eb646dee08da457d0e21683418914ceb17ce59b40aea495c327456aa" :answer/id #uuid "d6772212-08df-57a4-aa46-faccc338fc74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32671/selection/06091d4b286ad0d1c77c2e126e81b659b141c7a59c33eaf2919c69713fa0febe" :answer/id #uuid "3d005d91-5f07-5a77-89b8-76000a116fc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32671/selection/589b045885deca1b751337548014679ef2aad00cb5dfe368fcafc7abca07bddc" :answer/id #uuid "a638ac67-b4b7-5351-a3e8-120d6ad12482" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32671/selection/76c61d574a4de61d532d50ffd6d89dd5fbda933bbf44f368c07cecafd6bdbc59" :answer/id #uuid "b71b43e6-cf84-58b3-85be-05cfbaaa087c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32671/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b7728b0-6a69-57b1-a89d-e6e4f0d7ee54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32671/selection/9162a6f6012cb98addd8a583acc316883bc4458aaa2d646ae20ba3e2c826df8c" :answer-field/choices ["q-32671/selection/9162a6f6012cb98addd8a583acc316883bc4458aaa2d646ae20ba3e2c826df8c" "q-32671/selection/0d70bb18eb646dee08da457d0e21683418914ceb17ce59b40aea495c327456aa" "q-32671/selection/06091d4b286ad0d1c77c2e126e81b659b141c7a59c33eaf2919c69713fa0febe" "q-32671/selection/589b045885deca1b751337548014679ef2aad00cb5dfe368fcafc7abca07bddc" "q-32671/selection/76c61d574a4de61d532d50ffd6d89dd5fbda933bbf44f368c07cecafd6bdbc59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32671" :question/id #uuid "7c3924e4-a03d-5fb7-a5cd-f6c273cb45fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-32671" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=3 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =3, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-1+4{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1+4(3) \\\\  & =11, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =4-3{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =4-3(3)-2(11) \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -27\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32671/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32671"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105930/selection/1e2bc63edb71d65e5f0ad2b0b84b94763132fc4192942bf66eab13b4a19e6964" :answer/id #uuid "84a7c668-c6d9-5e60-8898-a2aa67042427" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105930/selection/4ccd751c9b2a75985b08bd206e8c19076cd1a680ede81144180356d430c8b994" :answer/id #uuid "32ad1aa6-86b1-5ef7-b68d-ff7b983268cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105930/selection/c400ac78981be475bfac5570d2a601f2f7f18adad55647391ee901cf239f2b88" :answer/id #uuid "c120872c-2781-5058-80be-f0dec35cef87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105930/selection/ce5d9ed5a72aeca987cd29848733b723b404aa1c901f2b9284e6fec6a6230300" :answer/id #uuid "d709fdcf-0cee-5ac2-a34a-8c0e487f30c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105930/selection/59a3645edbb46a5ebdb7f75f57cb10deddd5e69c8606ef749f849bfaccf1aacd" :answer/id #uuid "f702670b-f819-5e07-af5e-9b311b04e5e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105930/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23fd2f2e-4c2c-5598-b03f-bcf5f10743e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105930/selection/ce5d9ed5a72aeca987cd29848733b723b404aa1c901f2b9284e6fec6a6230300" :answer-field/choices ["q-105930/selection/1e2bc63edb71d65e5f0ad2b0b84b94763132fc4192942bf66eab13b4a19e6964" "q-105930/selection/4ccd751c9b2a75985b08bd206e8c19076cd1a680ede81144180356d430c8b994" "q-105930/selection/c400ac78981be475bfac5570d2a601f2f7f18adad55647391ee901cf239f2b88" "q-105930/selection/ce5d9ed5a72aeca987cd29848733b723b404aa1c901f2b9284e6fec6a6230300" "q-105930/selection/59a3645edbb46a5ebdb7f75f57cb10deddd5e69c8606ef749f849bfaccf1aacd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105930" :question/id #uuid "b49c135b-ee7c-514c-acd4-fa5185ae6537" :question/math-academy-id "q-105930" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-2 \\\\ 9{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2-9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2-9(-2) \\\\  & =16, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1+4{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1+4(-2)-(16) \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105930/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105930"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105951/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "b6de57ac-1896-5292-9c6e-d8ffa638a6aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105951/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "14ae2984-b59e-5742-9b76-668a651d69f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105951/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "4460d39c-46ba-5545-8a3d-56dd2b9297cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105951/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "26f8e74c-f5d6-5098-a661-a511e07688ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105951/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "59a3963c-d2c4-592c-ad81-30318af760f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105951/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e859a6a4-14d8-5c00-9c52-e8623c14f4cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105951/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-105951/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-105951/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-105951/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-105951/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-105951/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105951" :question/id #uuid "1861ef9a-574a-56cc-89ee-9ea58e347255" :question/math-academy-id "q-105951" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=6 \\\\ 4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=6$ and ${y}_{2}=-4.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{2}=(-1)\\cdot (-4)=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105951/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105951"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32570/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "3b09b760-8f1b-5fb2-a968-da0775ffefa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32570/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "271bcefe-4deb-51ab-9494-33415f491eaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32570/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "a8f3d211-3327-5a09-b4db-423cd5065931" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32570/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "f0f2072f-768a-56b1-9616-0b7e0993f827" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32570/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "2df462be-e488-5d12-b16f-f25d8b8f6061" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32570/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab533481-7486-5f37-8712-eebe8309d795" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32570/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-32570/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-32570/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-32570/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-32570/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-32570/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32570" :question/id #uuid "8eaf079f-b6a4-5f80-b8a8-2783953d0262" :question/math-academy-id "q-32570" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-4$ and ${y}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-4+3(-\\frac{2}{3})=-6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32570/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104861/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "d6b7909f-1434-5259-bfd8-8ab317acca69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104861/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "56c5bcfe-6205-516a-8e5c-62e6bb91a262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104861/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "a80cd910-3693-5f5c-8ef9-61565e976cc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104861/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "686b9bde-5fc4-5081-8505-1444454999b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104861/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "174bc5c5-2fdc-584d-a846-2c0dffae8daf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104861/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6179c6a6-401d-5aaf-a06a-dfeb3a7510c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104861/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-104861/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-104861/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-104861/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-104861/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-104861/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104861" :question/id #uuid "8b452cf4-4d72-5df1-88c6-867fd46459f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-104861" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions of the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of the product ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=1 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=1$ and ${y}_{2}=4.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 4=-6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104861/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104861"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105953/selection/631f51392e8a1c1f6caee2fe554fe81c00782fbf39c69cdefd00551fd32357e4" :answer/id #uuid "3028f5d5-fe41-5fee-81df-8ca8c4490ea1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{130}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105953/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" :answer/id #uuid "a1651cfe-7f95-52c3-a899-4b2098c85460" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105953/selection/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" :answer/id #uuid "a96fe158-7918-5827-a6bc-7956b8cafcf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105953/selection/d6e713f547840addea9eae5f85975430135abde0b8abf17cb48d405202b43b0b" :answer/id #uuid "dcb46c83-6082-52d5-9863-c7dc89f7326a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105953/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" :answer/id #uuid "9f929d96-7b48-5baa-9dfc-6c07b4b71fdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105953/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecdc2461-243e-5a09-bec5-42d4b5e7879e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105953/selection/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" :answer-field/choices ["q-105953/selection/631f51392e8a1c1f6caee2fe554fe81c00782fbf39c69cdefd00551fd32357e4" "q-105953/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" "q-105953/selection/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" "q-105953/selection/d6e713f547840addea9eae5f85975430135abde0b8abf17cb48d405202b43b0b" "q-105953/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105953" :question/id #uuid "af800076-1dc9-5a0d-bd5f-a7e1f437d795" :question/math-academy-id "q-105953" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=5$ and ${y}_{2}=14.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-7$ and ${x}_{1}=\\frac{26}{7}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{26}{7} \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}=\\frac{26}{7}\\cdot 14=52.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105953/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105953"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-105949"] :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-1 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-1$ and ${y}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=2$ and ${x}_{1}=-1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}=(-1)\\cdot (-1)=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8926"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/fd1cf7c3d929fb79576a59d4ef3aebd3f24a0d570c938ab80ebd44c5bd4c238f.png)\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/b521c0b31d05de273d0abd37e00b046c0e36ed47ef30d22784a24cace4d676f9.png)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 66\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ 15{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=5$ and $y_2=-9.$ \n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/ccb4ab47d3a270cf9545d4f79e6f90b944cf6121fca3752eeee6ddc712fcfdec.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4777"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/f88cbbb9459dd3b467e6b87d230ad23634461597aa9d8da3e933774273e2ab2f.png)\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/7704f9285f14f496bb9f1721d188866c9464c585e33235c5cc6eee42e3f3a3eb.png)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/712643d674cf8a7a086a9a935659d86bba7bd2fb25f131ec56e798cfc1d538d9.png)\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=2 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4 \\\\ {y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =4-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =4-(2) \\\\  & =2, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1-{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1-(2)+2(2) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/151dc664a131df0f3e13f2997bb1af6d41586b5f4dcf8a1acd1342f85e1b9c92.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4775"] :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b},$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/45cefb7311cd5253b76164cc7f2f3ce01b445f0e9061b720865227128b60debe.png)\nIf $\\langle x_1,x_2 \\rangle$ and $\\langle y_1,y_2 \\rangle$ are the solutions to the systems $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ and $L\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{b}$ respectively, what is the value of $x_1 \\cdot y_2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/b521c0b31d05de273d0abd37e00b046c0e36ed47ef30d22784a24cace4d676f9.png)\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/9dcc9f71745cce72ce7e122b3bc8cd7064d05f3be90d712202f42956956ef18e.png)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=6 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=6$ and $y_2=4.$ Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/903fbfe6828526dace264d65baebf58c31e36db8a54e25ed1f3be859e6079ebb.png)\n\n- Next, we solve $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/dcb234ae13cab2676ea5afa7fde452c870ff5088ff5748342c517bf2a96327a8.png)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $x_2=-2$ and $x_1=2.$ Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/assets/53bace542ba4dfd0d7e5e4bf9b6451c7f39502dd1bf24d030f654050629f0e0d.png)\n\nFinally, $x_1 \\cdot y_2 = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
